        "Footnote 1: maximum trailering ratings are intended for comparison purposes only; the weight of passengers, cargo and options or accessories may reduce the amount you can trailer.",
        "GCWR includes the weight of the vehicle and trailer combination, including driver, passengers, fuel, optional equipment and cargo.",
        "Maximum trailer weight rating = GCWR minus curb weight, with 150 lbs each for a driver and a front passenger (guide p. 7).",
        "When using a weight-carrying hitch, the maximum trailer weight is 5,000 lbs. with a 600-lb. trailer tongue weight. A weight-distributing hitch and sway control are required for trailer tongue weights greater than 600 lbs.",
        "Suburban and Tahoe: trailer tongue weight should be 10% to 15% of total loaded trailer weight (up to 1,250 lbs.); must not cause vehicle weights to exceed RGAWR or GVWR.",
        "The standard Heavy-Duty Trailering Package on Suburban and Tahoe includes an auxiliary external transmission fluid cooler and engine oil cooler.",
        "Table columns are Tahoe 2WD / Tahoe 4WD (Suburban columns not captured). No 2023 Tahoe document was available; 2023 skipped.",
        "maxTongueWD 1,250 = 'up to 1,250 lbs.' tongue figure combined with the statement that a weight-distributing hitch is required above 600 lbs.; maxTongueWC 600 from the weight-carrying hitch sentence (trailer limited to 5,000 lbs.)."
